<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav livestock breeders return to EU -- agency.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav livestock breeders return to EU -- agency.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yugoslav livestock breeders and exporters have returned to the corresponding European Union (EU) bodies, the Tanjug news agency reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>Their acceptance by the EU groups was brokered by the Yugoslav livestock fund, Stofo.</p>
<p>&quot;The decision was made on October 19 in Paris at a meeting of representatives of EU national communities of livestock and meat producers and traders,&quot; Milan Njegomir, Stofo director, was quoted by the agency as saying.</p>
<p>Njegomir said this decision was, &quot;vital for the return of Yugoslav livestock and meat exporters to EU markets&quot;.</p>
<p>He also said the former Yugoslavia's meat and livestock exports to the former European Community market stood at $350 million a year, and that Serbia and Montenegro, which make up the present Yugoslavia, accounted for almost half that figure.</p>
<p>-- Beti Bilandzic, Belgrade newsroom + 381 11 222 43 05</p>
</text>
